/-!
# B-line IL, `J` pre-table (B5-J), part 1: steps and triples on the register file

On top of the register file `RF v c` of `J6SegILPre2`:

* reads of arbitrary stacks: an expression may read a register of `rg` or the top of any
  non-empty stack outside `rg` (`Rd c e`); its value `ev v c e` does not depend on the base state;
* the elementary steps `sA` (assign a register), `sAo` (assign the top of a stack outside `rg`),
  `sU` (push), `sO` (pop), `sMv` (`mvK`), and `sRd` (random read of a list entry);
* Hoare triples `Tr p P Q C` (`∀ s`, from every `RF v c` with `P v c` to some `RF v' c'` with
  `Q v' c'`, cost `≤ C`), with `seq`, consequence and the counted loop `Tr.rep`.
-/

